ALVA — Roster UI Improvements, Discover Lore & Play-Style Rewrite

Objective

Make a focused, polished update to Alva’s roster presentation and Discover interface.

First, inspect the current repository, understand the existing UI architecture, character system, localization, navigation, and responsive design. Then implement all requested changes directly in the game.

This is a UI and editorial-content update, not a gameplay overhaul. Preserve Alva’s existing visual identity: dark charcoal surfaces, clean typography, subtle borders, restrained green accents, and consistent spacing.

The final result must work across desktop, mobile landscape, keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad.

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

1. All rosters — move character numbers to the bottom-right

Current implementation

The shared roster is implemented in:

* js/ui/fighter-roster.js
* js/ui/fighter-browser.js
* css/setup.css
* css/responsive.css

Each roster slot contains a .slot-num element currently positioned at the top-left. Available fighters also have a .slot-name strip across the bottom of their portrait.

Required changes

Move the character/slot number from the top-left to the bottom-right corner of every roster card.

Requirements:

* Apply the change to every roster that uses the shared component.
* Position the number neatly inside the card’s lower-right area.
* Keep consistent right and bottom spacing across all card sizes.
* Preserve the current numbering format.
* Ensure the number remains clearly visible and does not overlap the fighter’s name.
* If the number shares the bottom strip with the fighter’s name, reserve enough horizontal space for both.
* Keep fighter names aligned to the left and numbers aligned to the right.
* Apply the placement consistently to available, selected, locked, and disabled roster slots.
* Preserve the locked icons, selection checkmarks, portraits, focus rings, and accessibility labels.
* Do not hardcode positioning per fighter.

Use the shared component and styles rather than adding individual overrides to different screens.

Make the black name strip slightly transparent

The black/dark strip behind a character’s name currently looks too solid.

Make it slightly transparent, so the portrait remains subtly visible underneath it.

Design direction:

* Use a dark translucent background, approximately 75–85% opacity, adjusted to suit the existing theme.
* Keep the same general height and clean appearance.
* Maintain strong contrast for the name and character number.
* Do not reduce the opacity of the text itself.
* Do not make the strip heavily transparent or difficult to read.
* Keep the effect consistent across hover, focus, and selected states.

Only the background layer should become translucent.

Screens to cover

The change must appear everywhere the shared roster is used, including:

* Select Fighter.
* Custom Play’s Select CPU.
* Both Watch Mode CPU selection screens.
* Practice Ground’s Change Fighter roster.
* Practice Ground’s CPU selection roster.
* Discover → Fighters.

If another roster instance uses the same component, it must receive the update automatically.

