3. Rosters without Confirm — move “Read play style” fully to the bottom-right

Current implementation

The play-style button is generated by FighterRoster and currently uses:

* .play-style-action
* .text-action
* .preview-info
* .preview-info--no-confirm

The FighterBrowser subclass removes the Confirm button.

Required behavior

Whenever a roster does not have a Confirm character button, the Read play style action must sit at the very bottom-right of the character preview information area.

It should not float awkwardly immediately beneath the character name with unnecessary empty space below it.

Design requirements:

* Right-align the action.
* Anchor it visually at the bottom edge of the preview information area.
* Keep only a small, consistent amount of right and bottom padding.
* Preserve sufficient padding for its focus outline and touch target.
* Keep it separate from the fighter name and difficulty stars.
* Preserve the underlined, quiet secondary-action appearance.
* Maintain legibility when the translated label wraps.
* Avoid overlap with the animated fighter preview.
* Avoid using fragile absolute positioning that breaks at smaller resolutions.

Prefer a robust flex or grid arrangement.

Important distinction

Rosters with a Confirm button must remain different.

For Confirm-enabled rosters:

* Keep Read play style above Confirm.
* Preserve the existing Confirm button behavior.
* Maintain reasonable spacing between the two controls.
* Do not push the action below Confirm.

For rosters without Confirm:

* Read play style becomes the final, bottom-right action.
* Do not add an unnecessary empty button area.
* Do not introduce a Confirm button.

Implement this based on whether the roster has Confirm, not based on the screen name or character ID.

The existing .preview-info--no-confirm hook is a suitable place to start.

